WEBVTT

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.140
The water's so close!

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:22.740
The Dancer line is really popular because it offers a close-up view of the Sea of Izu.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:26.960
An ocean view, huh?

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.880
Doesn't really feel like
I'm looking at it from a train.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.540
These windows seem really big, too.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:34.630
Because they <i>are!</i>

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:37.920
This is the Dancer's panorama view!

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.920
In order to allow the customers to enjoy the fantastic scenery,

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.920
the sides of the cars were remodeled into boldly open windows!

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.260
Put a sock in it.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:54.660
R-Right.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:01:01.540
I-I'm sorry! We're so busy that she only has time to sleep en route to locations.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.420
You don't need to apologize to them.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:07.580
No one asked them to come along.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:13.460
Escorting a pop star?

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:15.950
One Ms. Noa Kashima.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.600
She's this year's JNR image girl.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:20.750
Who's that?

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.220
I dunno.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:25.140
Huh, she looks familiar.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:29.150
You don't even know the girl loved by everyone in Japan?

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:31.580
I don't watch TV.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:34.360
I just stick to informational programs.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:38.240
She's been in a lot of TV shows and commercials recently.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:45.100
And yet, despite her extremely busy schedule, she's graciously doing a JNR event in Izu.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.100
Basically, she's gonna give JNR a little boost in popularity!

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:57.320
I, Osamu Oominato, must take steps to ensure that nothing happens to Queen NoaвЂ”

00:01:58.390 --> 00:01:59.620
Noa?

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:00.550
Queen?

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:03.280
Member number seven, huh?

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:04.560
H-Hey!

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:05.620
Give that back!

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:08.440
I have some things to take care of.
You all go on ahead.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.180
Make sure to show her around.

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:13.750
Thank you for riding the Dancer special express.

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:16.900
So, why are we taking the train again?

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:18.160
Because, you know, we're working for JNR.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.300
We will soon be arriving in Ito.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.920
Makes sense.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.080
Trains are great! They really make you feel like you're on a trip!

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:29.140
Uh...

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:33.780
This train was named for the famous story <i>The Izu Dancer</i>.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:36.060
You've heard of it, right?

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:40.220
That was Noa's third movie.

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:42.620
You've been in movies?

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:44.000
Wow!

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.160
The Dancer must have been really cool onscreen!

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.820
The train wasn't in the movie.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:48.660
What?

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.400
Even I knew that.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.020
How can a movie called <i>The Izu Dancer</i>
not feature the Dancer train?

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.660
You really mean that, don't you?

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:56.520
But it's the Dancer!

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:57.780
And they're dancers!

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.860
Oh, Takayama.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.250
Those on track two, please watch out.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:39.380
The Dancer express with service to Izukyu-Shimoda has arrived.

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:41.010
Those on track two, please stand back.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.800
The Dancer is now stopping.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:48.850
Thank you for riding. This is Ito.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.980
Now to get this collection book stamped.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:00.940
Takayama.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:03.030
What?

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:04.780
Look at him.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.780
What about him?

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:10.700
U-Um, please...

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:12.950
Please take this!

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:16.290
Oh, of course. I canвЂ”

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:18.790
N-Not you!

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:19.880
Look out!

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:25.880
Ow, ow, ow!

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:26.840
What happened?
Ow, ow, ow!

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.680
Takayama!

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:44.780
I'll go with this swimsuit.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:47.490
Noa, listen to me.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:53.330
Excuse me, I'm Iida of the Tokyo Central Railway Security Force, Fourth Peacekeeper Squad.

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:57.040
I heard my subordinate, Takayama, was here.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:57.830
Oh.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.540
He's over there.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:00.920
Oh dear.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.670
Excuse me.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:05.970
N-Noa!

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:10.890
It's fine. He's out cold, right?

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:14.350
Besides, there's not much time.

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:19.600
Let's get the shoot over with
so I can rehearse for the concert.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.900
Are you really doing this?

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:23.440
Of course I am.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.440
I won't let anyone get in
the way of my concerts.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:33.160
They're talking about something important.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:36.830
Just remember what happened
right after we got to the station.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:38.410
You don't know what elseвЂ”

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:43.880
No matter the circumstances, a pro
always answers the fans' expectations.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:47.380
Um, has something happened?

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:51.180
This was in my bag.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.810
It's just another prank.

00:06:56.350 --> 00:07:01.520
And even if the threat's real, I'm still singing.

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:08.530
Um, we have to be at
a shoot for the CD jacket now.

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:09.780
Excuse us.

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:15.030
Oh, and Takayama, was it?

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:17.200
Can you give this to him when he wakes up?

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:22.380
As thanks for saving me.

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:30.720
Hear that?

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:39.980
Uh, I guess we should put all our efforts into searching and sterilizing the place.

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.690
Are we supposed to use
soap for that or something?

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:47.900
He means to check the area for
dangerous objects and suspicious behavior.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:52.700
Then if we find anything, remove it.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.160
Couldn't you just have said that?

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:59.700
You can't go around at a station or whatever and announce you're about to look for dangerous objects.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:01.910
What're you up to here?

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:12.430
A-Are you gonna sing in that?

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:16.390
The rehearsal is right after the shoot, so yeah.

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:18.890
Just a little extra tidbit for the fans, I guess.

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:21.060
We <i>are</i> at the beach, after all.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:25.270
Yeah, you gotta wear a swimsuit when you're at the beach.

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:26.480
Huh?

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:35.410
Aren't you just the least bit unsettled?

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:38.530
If you've got it, flaunt it.

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:40.910
You've got some nice curves, Sakurai.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:43.410
Flaunt it?

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:46.380
And this swimsuit is a little...

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:48.170
Really?

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:51.880
You're cute, so you should go for it.

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:56.090
Yes?

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:56.680
Nothing.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:00.220
You just seem to be flaunting it kinda well.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:04.440
Not really, no. I mean, it's just like how I sleep.

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:05.480
What?

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:07.900
Haruka, you sleep naked?!

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:09.730
Yeah.

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:12.530
Okay! Koumi, you can wear this.

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:16.450
I don't think there's enough material.

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:17.530
Really?

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.330
You're gonna pop out.

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:21.410
H-Hey, Aoi!

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:24.250
Both of you should use this chance to make an impression.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:25.080
Huh?

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.670
On who?

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.250
Gotcha!

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:31.920
Ms. Iida!

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:36.050
You're good! You're good!

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:39.090
There, there, there! OK!

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:44.890
What's up?

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.480
Nothing.

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:49.940
Seriously, nothing's happening.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:51.480
That's the point.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:54.820
I can't believe this.

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.910
Wait up, Aoi!

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:08.210
Come here, you.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:13.590
Takayama!

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:17.050
What're <i>you</i> looking at?

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:19.590
I-Is something off?

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:23.510
No, uh, I was just thinking
you two really stand out.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.560
That's the point!

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:29.850
This beach is way too large
for just us to patrol.

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:31.940
So we should stand out!

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:33.150
Sorry?

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:36.650
No criminal wants to get caught.

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:45.200
So if we boldly announce that we're here guarding Ms. Noa's concert, it'll make them think twice.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:47.120
Is that how it works?

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:53.130
It worked pretty well when Hitomi and I tried it in the past, at least.

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:06.640
Noey, can you see the tape at the center of the stage?

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.060
Must be this.

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:25.080
Find anything?

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:28.500
Not a single singe mark.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:33.500
This guy must have mixed in flash paper with the confetti.

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:35.750
Flash paper?

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:37.250
Watch.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:47.560
I'm fine. It's bright and big,
but the flame burns out in an instant.

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:49.430
You don't get burnt.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:52.350
They use it in magic.

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:54.440
It's not very dangerous.

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:57.650
Why'd someone do this?

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:01.950
My guess would be as a warning or a threat.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:06.620
The event tomorrow might
actually be really dangerous.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:09.450
We just have to catch the bastard first.

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:11.660
Easier said than done!

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:13.210
Grab 'em on sight, huh?

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:15.210
Stop the concert?

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:17.210
Are you crazy?

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:18.420
That is <i>not</i> happening!

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:20.420
But if something happensвЂ”

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:21.720
I'm not running away.

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:25.590
In any case, stopping the concert is impossible at this point.

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:28.180
Let's just all do our jobs.

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:38.520
I can't help but worry.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:41.900
Who knows what will happen?

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:44.410
Worrying's just gonna give you wrinkles.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:48.910
You're in danger! We really
should stop the concert.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:53.410
I'm not going to let them beat me.

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:56.250
Safety first, remember?

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.380
Uh...

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.090
I see I misjudged you.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:04.300
W-Wait!

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:12.730
Takayama!

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:15.850
You do realize where you are, right?

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:18.230
S-Sorry!

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:20.820
Ow.

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:24.110
What's this?

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:29.780
Invading the women's bath.

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:32.040
You sure are amazing, Takayama.

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:38.580
Why is everyone telling me
to step off the stage?

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:45.760
Takayama's just really worried about you, Ms. Noa.

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:54.310
Here.

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:57.190
That's a lot.

00:13:57.190 --> 00:14:00.270
My old man always said to
nip danger in the bud.

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:02.820
What's this?

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:04.990
You need to be prepared against snakebite, right?

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:06.900
Your dad seems like a piece of work.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:02.460
I feel a little better now.

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:09.590
When I first started singing on the street, no one ever paused to listen.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:15.180
But I never stopped singing,
and it's brought me all the way here.

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:19.390
So I won't stop singing.

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:21.900
No matter what happens,
I'll sing my heart out!

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:40.460
Noa, I love you!

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:47.500
The JNR summer special,
Noa Kashima in Izu, will now begin!

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:19.680
She really gets your adrenaline going.

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:21.270
Yeah.

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:33.190
How you doing, guys?

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:36.910
Great!

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:40.120
Let's enjoy the heck out of today!

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:46.000
Everyone here sure is fired up!

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:48.500
Huh?

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:51.000
Ms. Iida and Ms. Nanao?

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:56.840
You see, Ms. Noa's been named
JNR Public Security Force Captain-For-A-Day.

00:17:57.380 --> 00:18:00.010
Oh! That explains these clothes.

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:05.020
I had no idea why I was wearing them until this moment!

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:09.480
There.

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:12.110
You're making me blush.

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:15.900
So, Ms. Noa, how did you get here?

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:17.530
By train, of course!

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:20.030
It's a JNR event, after all.

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.290
You don't mean to tell me...

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:27.540
I love the rails!

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:30.580
Long ago, I would bring my guitar on the train, and it was like it was taking me to the stage of my dreams.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:32.290
Who's that?

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:33.500
What's he up to?

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:33.960
Long ago, I would bring my guitar on the train, and it was like it was taking me to the stage of my dreams.

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:34.960
Is that a staff member?

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:36.380
I see!

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:39.630
Oh, right! He used the confetti as cover!

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:41.850
And the only people who could do that...

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:44.060
are the staff!

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:46.220
Thank you!

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:48.100
What?

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:51.860
Wh-What do you think you're doing?

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.360
Oh dear!

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:56.860
A nasty villain has shown up!

00:18:56.860 --> 00:18:59.240
But never fear!

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:03.240
The JNR Public Security Force will protect Ms. Noa!

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:05.740
Ms. Iida, that's the actual criminal!

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:06.500
I know.

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:08.250
What?!

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:11.750
It'd be more dangerous to send all these people into a panic.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.000
You're right.

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:16.800
Oh no! I'm in real trouble!

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:22.840
So, as Captain-For-A-Day, I order you to protect me from that man!

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:24.300
Damn it all!

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:28.980
Look out!

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:41.320
Takayama!

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:50.040
Takayama!

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:54.210
Wow, that hurt!

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:56.420
Did you catch him?

00:19:56.420 --> 00:19:57.210
Huh?

00:19:57.210 --> 00:19:58.550
Y-Yeah.

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:02.800
Captain! Mission complete!

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:07.310
Good work!

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:08.810
Nice job, PSF!

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:11.020
Noa, you're so cool!

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:13.520
I wish I could have let loose.

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:15.060
Don't be crazy.

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:30.370
Man, that really hurt.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:35.330
There's a hole in my stamp collection book!

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:37.340
You shouldn't put yourself in danger like that.

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:38.880
Sorry.

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:42.800
Still, we managed to avoid
the audience panicking.

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:44.430
That's great.

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:47.260
Couldn't you have
thought of another way?

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:49.560
It was all so sudden.

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:52.140
Oh, right.

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:54.520
Thank you for the stamp book.

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:58.270
It's got a hole in it now,
but it saved my life.

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:01.530
Thanks!

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:07.030
Thank you too.

00:21:07.030 --> 00:21:07.870
Huh?

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:09.620
It's nothing!

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:24.970
Thank you for riding the Dancer today.

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:25.840
Noa.

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:26.470
Thank you for riding the Dancer today.

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:28.550
Here's your dinner.

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:30.390
Thanks.

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:34.270
Look out!

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:37.020
Thanks for the stamp book.

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:43.030
He works so hard for others.

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:48.070
I think I'm in love.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:51.240
With who?

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:57.540
The Dancer.

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:47.230
The JNR Ashio Line runs from the famous
mining town of Ashio, Tochigi to Kiryu, Gunma.

00:23:47.230 --> 00:23:51.610
Seeing those powerful KiHa 52 twin engines that can take the steep inclines of mountains

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:55.240
and valleys like nothing brings a tear to the eye!

